  "full_response": "# Fibonacci Sequence with Dynamic Programming in Python\n\nHere's a Python function that calculates the Fibonacci sequence using dynamic programming (memoization) to improve efficiency:\n\n```python\ndef fibonacci(n, memo={}):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the nth Fibonacci number using dynamic programming (memoization).\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The position in the Fibonacci sequence (0-based)\n        memo (dict): Dictionary to store computed values (used internally)\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The nth Fibonacci number\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n    memo[n] = fibonacci(n-1, memo) + fibonacci(n-2, memo)\n    return memo[n]\n\n# Example usage:\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    for i in range(10):\n        print(f\"Fibonacci({i}) = {fibonacci(i)}\")\n```\n\n## Alternative Implementation (Tabulation)\n\nHere's another dynamic programming approach using tabulation (bottom-up):\n\n```python\ndef fibonacci_tabulation(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the nth Fibonacci number using dynamic programming (tabulation).\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The position in the Fibonacci sequence (0-based)\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The nth Fibonacci number\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n\n    # Initialize a table to store Fibonacci numbers\n    fib = [0] * (n + 1)\n    fib[1] = 1\n\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        fib[i] = fib[i-1] + fib[i-2]\n\n    return fib[n]\n\n# Example usage:\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    for i in range(10):\n        print(f\"Fibonacci({i}) = {fibonacci_tabulation(i)}\")\n```\n\n## Key Features:\n\n1. **Memoization (Top-down approach)**:\n   - Stores previously computed results to avoid redundant calculations\n   - Uses recursion with a dictionary to cache results\n   - Time complexity: O(n)\n   - Space complexity: O(n)\n\n2. **Tabulation (Bottom-up approach)**:\n   - Builds the solution iteratively from smaller subproblems\n   - Uses an array to store intermediate results\n   - Time complexity: O(n)\n   - Space complexity: O(n) (can be optimized to O(1))\n\n",
